# mandatory-validation-gate-compliance

Validation and quality-gate outcomes are non-negotiable. Rework requests from a validation authority must never be refused or silently skipped; after rework the unit must re-enter the validation gate. The assembly loop is always closed by a successful validation, not declared complete on first assembly.

## Procedures
- After completing assembly, submit the unit to the Validation Engineer (Agent C) for inspection.
- If validation passes, proceed to the next workflow step.
- If validation rejects the unit, accept the rework request unconditionally.
- Execute the rework loop: disassemble only affected components, correct the defect, reassemble, and resubmit.
- Repeat until validation passes; do not exit the loop early.

## Conventions
- Rework requests must not be refused regardless of rework cost or inconvenience.
- Validation is always the final gate before a unit is considered complete.

